





Update only the existing unit test that verifies
context activation cleanup when a managed
onTestSuccess callback throws an exception.

The implementation now uses deferred invocation
cleanup.

Requirements:

1. Configure the managed callback to throw
   an intentional exception.

2. Verify the exception is propagated according
   to the existing callback contract.

3. Verify the temporary context activation is
   always closed, even when the callback throws.

4. Verify the ScopeCursor is restored to its
   previous state.

5. Verify the INVOCATION context remains
   registered after the failed callback.

6. Verify the context can still be resolved
   using its original UUID.

7. Simulate onFinish() for the owning TestNG
   context.

8. Verify the invocation is released afterward.

9. Verify the tracker is empty and no orphan
   invocation layers remain.

10. Do not modify production code.

11. Do not modify other tests.

12. Preserve all existing exception handling
    and lifecycle safety assertions.

Run only the updated test and report the result.
